# Runtime upload dirs created by storage-service / publication-client / trigger-client
# integration tests - populated on test runs, never committed.
backend/*/uploads/

# Local dev scratch (heap dumps, deploy logs, ws-events captures, systemd unit edits)
tmp/

# Per-session test-run logs (worktree scratch, never committed)
.testlogs/

# JWT signing keys - generated at first boot (JwtKeyPairManager / ce-entrypoint.sh).
# A real private key was historically committed here; never commit key material.
backend/monolith-service/data/keys/*.key
# Same generator, other host: auth-service writes ./data/keys relative to its working
# directory, so ANY local run of the service (or of its integration tests) leaves an RSA
# private key sitting untracked in the tree. This repo is exported to a public mirror,
# and that export is deny-list based - a stray `git add -A` would publish it.
backend/auth-service/data/

# Local TLS-interception CA for Docker builds (per-machine, see monolith Dockerfile)
backend/build-ca.pem

# Root-level dev scratch - one-off analysis scripts, API/response dumps, test
# screenshots, prod backfill/e2e SQL, foreign-code backups. Regenerated locally,
# never committed (removed wholesale in chore/repo-clutter-cleanup). Anchored to the
# repo root so legitimate same-named files under scripts/ etc. stay tracked.
#
# The rules below are by CLASS, not by name. The per-name list that follows them
# did not stop 126 new screenshots and Playwright dumps from landing at the root,
# because every new session invents new filenames. Anchoring to "/" keeps
# frontend/public/**, docs/** and every nested asset tracked as before.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp
/*.gif
/*.svg
# Root markdown is scratch by default. The negations below are the project's actual root
# docs. The public CE README is generated from deploy/ce-export/public-assets/README.public.md,
# not from a root README.
#
# The four CE files are NOT optional: deploy/ce-export/public-root-manifest.txt names them
# as expected roots of the published repo. GATE E (check-public-roots.sh) only flags
# UNEXPECTED roots, never missing ones, so without these negations it reports OK while a
# fresh clone or a repo re-seed publishes the public CE repo with no attribution, no
# trademark notice and no security policy.
/*.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/WORKTREE_CONVENTIONS.md
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!/TRADEMARKS.md
/analyze_*.py
/final_analysis.py
/final_report.py
/jit_feasibility.py
/help_form.json
/marketplace-response.json
/avatar-response-body.bin
/avatar-user-*.png
/otter.png
/seal.png
/mcp_image_*.png
/backfill_*.sql
/delete_nonnumeric_orphans.sql
/e2e-epoch-refresh.sql
/.claude_e2e_*.sql
/audit/

# Generated TypeScript view of node-contracts.schema.json (shared/contracts/scripts/
# generate-ts.js). Write-only: nothing imports it, and CI gates the schema through
# contracts:validate:strict + contracts:test instead. Ignored so a stray `git add -A`
# in a worktree cannot re-commit it and recreate the illusion of a drift gate.
frontend/app/workflows/builder/contracts/

# Playwright scratch captures written by e2e specs
frontend/e2e/.artifacts/

# Vendor OpenAPI documents harvested by scripts/api-migrations/tools. Deliberately
# not committed: they are large, they are the vendor's to change, and each recipe
# records the `specUrl` that fetches it again.
scripts/api-migrations/tools/_specs/
